    "text": "Two short bar magnets of dipole moments&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math> are joined at right angles to form a cross as depicted in the figure. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>θ</mi></math>&nbsp;for which the system remains in equilibrium in a uniform external magnetic field&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>,&nbsp;is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/WhatsApp_Image_2020-06-15_at_3.19.57_PM.jpeg\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 186px;\" />",
